(a) "Act" means the Insurance Act, 1938 (4 of 1938) as amended from time to time. 

_(b)_ "Authority" means the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India established under sub-section ( 1) of Section (3) of the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India Act, 1999; 

(c) "family" means a unit comprising of husband, wife, dependant parents and maximum of three children: 

Provided that where the number of children is more than three, for construing the composition of family as ·aforesaid, the first three children shall be included: 

Provided further that an insurer may, within the aforesaid parameters laid down for the composition of the family, define 'family' as per the requirements of the individual or group; 

_(d)_ "general micro-insurance product" means any health insurance contract, any contract covering the belongings, such as, hut, livestock or tools or instruments or any personal accident contract, either on individual or group basis, as per tenns stated in Schedule I of these regulations; 

